==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~6 seconds<sup>100f~180f</sup>.
*10 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 4.67~10 seconds<sup>140f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 40~53.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gory Dark|Gory Darks]] spawn, delay 30~43.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,300f</sup>.
**3 [[Gory Dark|Gory Darks]] spawn, delay 2~3.33 seconds<sup>60f~100f</sup>.
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Fight this stage as if it were [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Attack on W-Cyclone]]. Something to keep in mind is that Dark Emperor Nyandam doesn't really do much as a support enemy, unlike [[THE SLOTH]] in Attack on W-Cyclone. The Dark Cyclone is also very weak (in terms of attack power) compared to most other Cyclones.

An easy way to cheese this stage is to stack Anti-Dark/Floating Crowd Controllers on the starting peons before allowing the boss to spawn and get demolished with ease.

Another method would be to get [[Pizza Cat]] (true form is best), and if you have her, [[Mama Mummy Sumo]]. By using them together with your main damage dealers, Dark Cyclone will be locked in an endless knockback cycle, pinned onto the base, until it dies. When Dark Cyclone dies, the base will quickly die, and usually Nyandam is behind the base but doesn't do anything. Whether Nyandam dies or not, when the Cyclone dies, the base will quickly fall.

[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]] or [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] can trivialize this stage, as they can keep the cyclone permanently frozen so your heavy hitters can whittle it down.

